1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:23,200
To pray is to open your heart to God, to lift your heart and mind to the Father, to partner

2
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:32,320
with Jesus, to bend the arc of human history in the direction of the Kingdom.

3
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:41,120
To pray is to do something with the Spirit, and for the Spirit to do something in us.

4
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:47,620
To speak and to listen.

5
00:00:47,620 --> 00:01:04,300
To pray is to commune with a God who is closer to us than we are to ourselves.

6
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:07,200
Well, good morning, Canvas Community Church.

7
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:08,940
For those of you that haven't met me yet, my name is Ryan.

8
00:01:08,940 --> 00:01:11,500
I have the privilege of being one of the pastors here.

9
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:16,460
So grateful for that time of worship and that invitation to acknowledge God's presence

10
00:01:16,460 --> 00:01:18,460
in this place.

11
00:01:18,460 --> 00:01:24,620
All of the Bible is about the fact that the God who created the universe desires us to

12
00:01:24,620 --> 00:01:26,900
be in His presence.

13
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:30,520
He created us for relationship with Him.

14
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:35,740
And ever since the beginning, the story goes, we've been rebelling and choosing other things

15
00:01:35,740 --> 00:01:39,540
to find pleasure and satisfaction in.

16
00:01:39,540 --> 00:01:44,780
And if you're anything like me, you've probably tried a lot of things and many things have fallen

17
00:01:44,780 --> 00:01:45,220
short.

18
00:01:45,220 --> 00:01:52,660
And so, man, we're in this new series called Practicing the Way, which really is about habits

19
00:01:52,660 --> 00:01:56,520
that allow us to be in the presence of God.

20
00:01:56,520 --> 00:02:01,940
We've been spending four weeks on prayer, and it's really a practice-based discipleship.

21
00:02:01,940 --> 00:02:06,480
It's intentional, it's aimed at spending time in the presence of God.

22
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:15,100
And the American church, and even just post-enlightenment, I feel like has maybe overvalued intellectual

23
00:02:15,100 --> 00:02:21,900
discipleship and to the detriment of relational-based discipleship.

24
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:26,480
And so throughout the time, throughout the next three years, really, we're going to look

25
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:32,160
at nine practices from the life and teachings of Jesus, aimed at helping us get into the

26
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:33,020
presence of God.

27
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:39,700
And I just want to be super clear here that, like, this is not some legalistic type of thing

28
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:44,040
that, like, you check the right boxes, you put in the right equation, and then God rewards

29
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:44,180
you.

30
00:02:44,180 --> 00:02:49,480
The practices really are just aimed at you spending time with God.

31
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:54,440
And for any of us that have spent any time in the presence of God, we know that that is

32
00:02:54,440 --> 00:02:55,780
where transformation happens.

33
00:02:55,780 --> 00:02:57,880
I love how John Mark Homer puts it.

34
00:02:57,880 --> 00:03:03,040
He says, practices can't transform me into a person of Christ-like character.

35
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:08,900
These habits, these practices, these things we're inviting you to participate in, they can't

36
00:03:08,900 --> 00:03:12,500
do anything to transform you into a person of Christ-like character.

37
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:18,480
All they can do is open up a deeper part of yourself to the power and presence of God.

38
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:24,080
The power and presence of God does the transformative work in our hearts and our minds.

39
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:30,520
So that's our goal, is to spend time in the presence of God and allow the Holy Spirit to

40
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:32,500
transform our hearts and our minds.

41
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:36,140
So far, we've talked about prayer as talking to God.

42
00:03:36,140 --> 00:03:40,360
We've talked about quoting liturgy, praying the Scriptures, talked about the Lord's Prayer

43
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:44,760
and using the Lord's Prayer as a model for how we pray to God.

44
00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:53,160
We've talked about talking with God, through praise, through lament, which we're not often

45
00:03:53,160 --> 00:03:53,860
good at, right?

46
00:03:53,860 --> 00:03:55,360
We hide our anger from God.

47
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:56,960
We withdraw from God when we're angry.

48
00:03:56,960 --> 00:03:59,180
But God is not scared of our anger.

49
00:03:59,180 --> 00:04:01,100
He's not scared of our frustration and our pain.

50
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:04,500
We talk to God through praise, lament, petition, and intercession.

51
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:06,740
We ask for what we need and for what others need.

52
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:11,700
Last week, Sean talked about listening, quieting ourselves before God, allowing God to speak

53
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:12,980
to us.

54
00:04:12,980 --> 00:04:19,800
And today, we will just talk about being with God, being in the presence of God.

55
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:26,580
There's actually certain sects of Orthodox Jews that don't allow this praise, lament, petition

56
00:04:26,580 --> 00:04:32,740
type prayer on the Sabbath because it feels too much like work, like we're laboring with

57
00:04:32,740 --> 00:04:35,620
God to try and get something done, to see something accomplished.

58
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:40,780
And so there's this type of prayer that just allows ourselves to acknowledge God's presence

59
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:42,480
and be with him.

60
00:04:42,480 --> 00:04:44,100
No agenda.

61
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:47,560
Giving him space to do what he can only do.

62
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:49,360
So that's kind of our goal for this morning.

63
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:50,000
Sound like a plan?

64
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,860
Okay, let me pray and then we'll hop in.

65
00:04:52,860 --> 00:04:56,360
Father, we acknowledge your presence in this place.

66
00:04:58,020 --> 00:05:04,920
We know that your Holy Spirit is here and we expect him to do what only he can do.

67
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:12,420
God, prepare our minds and our hearts to hear from you, to receive something from you, and

68
00:05:12,420 --> 00:05:16,440
to accept your invitation into a deeper walk with you.

69
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:19,840
God, everything this world has to offer falls short.

70
00:05:20,580 --> 00:05:25,840
Everything our culture is going to celebrate tonight in the Super Bowl is fine and good,

71
00:05:25,840 --> 00:05:27,280
but it all falls short.

72
00:05:27,280 --> 00:05:31,980
It's all worshiping something less than what we were created to worship.

73
00:05:31,980 --> 00:05:38,080
And so as we consume content with our culture today, may we see it for what it is.

74
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:42,020
It's a game that you've given us that we can enjoy.

75
00:05:42,420 --> 00:05:47,580
But at the end of the day, if we put our stock, our worship, and what this world has to offer,

76
00:05:47,580 --> 00:05:48,620
we will come up short.

77
00:05:48,620 --> 00:05:53,220
So today, Father, may we acknowledge your presence in deeper ways.

78
00:05:53,220 --> 00:05:56,060
May we accept your invitation.

79
00:05:56,060 --> 00:06:00,920
God, may we draw near to you and may you draw near to us.

80
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:02,640
It's in Jesus' name I pray.

81
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:03,600
Amen.

82
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:09,200
If you want to follow along with me in your Bible, I'm going to be in Psalm 46 throughout

83
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:09,820
the time.

84
00:06:09,820 --> 00:06:11,880
I'm also just going to quote a lot of Scripture today.

85
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:13,440
Does that sound like a good plan to people?

86
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:15,420
Okay, good.

87
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:16,340
Yes, always.

88
00:06:16,340 --> 00:06:22,940
And just as a disclaimer, I've had a question or two from people throughout the past week

89
00:06:22,940 --> 00:06:27,240
or two about specifically this topic that we're going to be talking about today, contemplative

90
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:29,540
prayer, and about whether or not it's biblical.

91
00:06:29,540 --> 00:06:31,560
And I think that it is.

92
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:34,360
And I'm going to quote a lot of Scripture to try and prove it.

93
00:06:34,360 --> 00:06:38,320
I just want to let anybody know that if you're struggling or wrestling with any of the concepts

94
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:45,180
that are shared from stage, I, our elder board, our governance board, we'd love to chat with

95
00:06:45,180 --> 00:06:47,460
you and wrestle with you about what the Scriptures say.

96
00:06:47,460 --> 00:06:51,700
And that iron would sharpen iron, that we would become more like Christ together.

97
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:54,460
So that's just a disclaimer up front.

98
00:06:55,180 --> 00:06:59,540
I'm not going to make you raise your hands this week because it's a little heavy.

99
00:06:59,540 --> 00:07:02,120
Sometimes I make you raise your hands, but I don't want to embarrass you.

100
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:07,800
But hypothetically speaking, if I were to ask if anybody in the room is feeling anxious,

101
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:17,580
stressed out, or overwhelmed, would any of us be brave enough to raise our hands, right?

102
00:07:18,420 --> 00:07:22,380
Let me give a couple of examples of some things that might be stressing us out.

103
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:30,720
Any rejection of close relationships, any relational tension that any of you are dealing with.

104
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:32,540
Again, I won't make you raise your hand, but just think.

105
00:07:32,540 --> 00:07:40,880
Is there any relational tension, any familial relationships that have been severed that is weighing on you?

106
00:07:41,880 --> 00:07:51,320
Any stress from your career, success, aspirations, anybody got imposter syndrome in their job,

107
00:07:51,320 --> 00:07:53,540
or even just as being an adult?

108
00:07:53,540 --> 00:07:56,680
Anybody feel like you're just pretending and hoping nobody knows?

109
00:07:56,680 --> 00:08:00,520
Anybody in here lost a loved one recently?

110
00:08:00,520 --> 00:08:07,140
Anybody in here fear being punished for standing up for what's right?

111
00:08:07,140 --> 00:08:09,920
Some of us who work in secular environments,

112
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:13,260
we might feel like there are certain things that we just can't go along with.

113
00:08:13,260 --> 00:08:15,960
And if we don't go along with those things,

114
00:08:15,960 --> 00:08:19,500
we might not be able to get where we want to go in our career.

115
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:27,000
Or just the busyness of seemingly unending daily to-do lists.

116
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,220
Any moms in the room get to the end of the day

117
00:08:29,220 --> 00:08:31,740
and realize that you didn't eat anything all day this week?

118
00:08:31,740 --> 00:08:33,820
Anybody brave enough?

119
00:08:33,820 --> 00:08:35,900
Like, we're going to talk about fasting over the next couple weeks.

120
00:08:35,900 --> 00:08:37,140
Some of the moms in the room are like,

121
00:08:37,140 --> 00:08:40,100
I do that on accident sometimes.

122
00:08:40,100 --> 00:08:48,220
How about all of the above converging into one overly stressed out moment of life?

123
00:08:48,220 --> 00:08:50,000
Well, believe it or not,

124
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:56,200
these are the exact circumstances that Jesus and his disciples are facing all at the same time.

125
00:08:56,420 --> 00:08:58,260
In the book of Mark, chapter 6,

126
00:08:58,260 --> 00:09:03,000
the disciples have dealt with all of this stuff going on.

127
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,480
Jesus is rejected in his hometown of Nazareth.

128
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:08,120
His family and his friends push him out of town,

129
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:10,500
threatening to stone him and kill him.

130
00:09:12,580 --> 00:09:17,420
John the Baptist's cousin and close friend gets his head chopped off by Roman authorities.

131
00:09:17,420 --> 00:09:23,780
The disciples go out two by two and they have incredible success.

132
00:09:23,780 --> 00:09:25,560
They're healing people.

133
00:09:25,560 --> 00:09:26,700
They're casting out demons.

134
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:30,460
They're having all of this success and they're dealing with all of the emotional waves

135
00:09:30,460 --> 00:09:32,300
of what God is doing in and through them.

136
00:09:32,300 --> 00:09:35,360
Maybe pressure to take credit for some of that.

137
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:40,600
And then there's just so many crowds gathering around them.

138
00:09:40,600 --> 00:09:42,480
It says that they didn't even have time to eat.

139
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:48,500
And it's in that context that my slides are a little ahead,

140
00:09:48,500 --> 00:09:50,520
so it might be giving it away to you a little bit.

141
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:56,920
But it's in that context that the God of the universe doesn't make the sun stand still,

142
00:09:56,920 --> 00:09:59,540
which he's done in the past and could do if he wanted to, right?

143
00:09:59,540 --> 00:10:03,000
Give us a few extra hours in the day, a little bit more time.

144
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,840
He doesn't raise John the Baptist from the dead,

145
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:07,760
which we know he has the power to do.

146
00:10:08,800 --> 00:10:13,220
He doesn't crush his enemies or flip tables over this time.

147
00:10:13,220 --> 00:10:20,820
He doesn't even recruit more disciples to make the load a little bit easier on the ones that he has.

148
00:10:20,820 --> 00:10:22,200
What does he do?

149
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:23,740
He says this in Mark chapter 6.

150
00:10:23,740 --> 00:10:30,060
After all of the stress and anxiety and tension and emotional trauma of a difficult season in ministry,

151
00:10:30,060 --> 00:10:37,180
he says come away by yourselves to a lonely place and rest a while.

152
00:10:37,180 --> 00:10:43,800
Come away with me by yourselves to a lonely place and we'll rest a while.

153
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:48,640
In the midst of what has been one of the most difficult, emotionally draining seasons of the disciples' life,

154
00:10:48,760 --> 00:10:49,900
Jesus' invitation.

155
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:57,580
Anybody brave enough to say that with me?

156
00:10:57,580 --> 00:10:59,440
And yet here's the deal.

157
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:03,120
There's saints in here who have been following Jesus for a long time,

158
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:07,960
who have walked through some of the darkest seasons that any of us could ever imagine.

159
00:11:08,920 --> 00:11:12,000
And if I gave them the opportunity to come up here and testify,

160
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:16,980
they would say that God's presence is all they needed in the midst of that difficult challenge.

161
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:22,420
See, we live in a cultural moment that's busier than ever.

162
00:11:22,420 --> 00:11:25,940
Technology was supposed to make our lives more efficient,

163
00:11:25,940 --> 00:11:27,520
which was supposed to give us more free time,

164
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:33,320
which we were supposed to use to rest, relax, invest in important relationships,

165
00:11:33,320 --> 00:11:35,640
you know, be good humans.

166
00:11:35,640 --> 00:11:37,340
But what did we do instead?

167
00:11:37,340 --> 00:11:41,540
We took the efficiency and we made ourselves more busy.

168
00:11:41,540 --> 00:11:47,720
We invested ourselves in more things and we are over busy and hurried like crazy.

169
00:11:48,660 --> 00:11:51,440
And even if your personal life is going pretty good,

170
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:56,200
you add unnecessary stress and anxiety and worry to your life

171
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:59,060
by doing what I call the death scroll, right?

172
00:11:59,060 --> 00:12:03,560
You're filling your mind and your heart with the burdens and stresses and anxieties

173
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:05,120
of people that you don't even know.

174
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:11,840
And in the midst of all of this stress and worry and anxiety and hurry,

175
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:17,200
Christ's invitation to you, I believe, is the same as his invitation to his disciples

176
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:21,100
when they found themselves stressed, overwhelmed, anxious, hurried.

177
00:12:21,100 --> 00:12:24,620
Come away to a lonely place.

178
00:12:24,620 --> 00:12:26,320
Be with me.

179
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:28,780
Rest in my presence.

180
00:12:28,780 --> 00:12:32,360
So this is what we're talking about this morning.

181
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:35,900
This type of prayer that's aimed at resting in God's presence,

182
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:38,200
inviting God's presence into your life,

183
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:41,720
and just relaxing into the grace of God.

184
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:44,480
Without words at times.

185
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:47,320
And throughout history, it's been called different things at different times.

186
00:12:47,320 --> 00:12:52,020
In the presence of God, who made you, loves you.

187
00:12:52,020 --> 00:12:52,720
And listen to this.

188
00:12:52,720 --> 00:12:56,220
He is sovereign over all of your fear, anxiety, and worry.

189
00:12:56,220 --> 00:12:59,900
You cannot add an extra moment to your life by worrying.

190
00:13:00,060 --> 00:13:05,900
So what if we just took God's invitation to heart and we just got away for a few minutes?

191
00:13:05,900 --> 00:13:07,160
And I know how hard this sounds.

192
00:13:07,160 --> 00:13:07,680
Believe me.

193
00:13:07,680 --> 00:13:09,240
I've tried it the past couple of weeks.

194
00:13:09,240 --> 00:13:11,040
And with 10 months old, it's difficult.

195
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:11,860
It's challenging.

196
00:13:11,860 --> 00:13:19,580
But what if we just got five minutes a day to just get away and rest in the presence of God?

197
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:23,260
Psalm chapter 91, verses 1 through 10 says this.

198
00:13:23,260 --> 00:13:29,740
Those who live in the shelter of the Most High will find rest in the shadow of the Almighty.

199
00:13:29,740 --> 00:13:31,580
Does that sound good to anybody this morning?

200
00:13:31,580 --> 00:13:34,760
This I declare about the Lord.

201
00:13:34,760 --> 00:13:37,800
He alone is my refuge, my place of...

202
00:13:37,800 --> 00:13:38,960
I declare about the Lord.

203
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:42,320
He alone is my refuge, my place of safety.

204
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:44,580
He is my God, and I trust Him.

205
00:13:44,580 --> 00:13:50,960
For He will rescue you from every trap and protect you from every deadly disease.

206
00:13:50,960 --> 00:13:53,880
We should have read that in 2020 a bit more.

207
00:13:53,880 --> 00:13:56,720
He will cover you with His feathers.

208
00:13:56,720 --> 00:14:04,360
This intimate, relational picture of a mother hen embracing her chicks under her wings.

209
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:05,980
He will shelter you with His wings.

210
00:14:05,980 --> 00:14:08,640
His faithful promises are your armor and your protection.

211
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:12,900
Do not be afraid of the terrors of the night nor the arrow that flies in the day.

212
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:17,460
Do not dread the disease that stalks in darkness, nor the disaster that strikes at midday.

213
00:14:17,460 --> 00:14:21,960
Though a thousand fall at your side, though ten thousand are dying around you,

214
00:14:21,960 --> 00:14:23,640
these evils will not touch you.

215
00:14:23,640 --> 00:14:24,280
Listen to this.

216
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:27,120
Just open your eyes.

217
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:33,200
Acknowledge God's presence, His sovereignty over all of your stress, worry, and anxiety,

218
00:14:33,200 --> 00:14:34,740
and see how the wicked are punished.

219
00:14:34,740 --> 00:14:37,160
If you make the Lord your refuge,

220
00:14:37,160 --> 00:14:39,540
if you make the Most High your shelter,

221
00:14:39,540 --> 00:14:42,320
no evil will conquer you.

222
00:14:42,900 --> 00:14:46,020
So I've been thinking about contemplative prayer a lot the past couple of weeks.

223
00:14:46,020 --> 00:14:48,180
Different people talk about it in different ways,

224
00:14:48,180 --> 00:14:52,500
and some people seem to kind of indicate that this is,

225
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:59,000
that it takes a level of spiritual maturity to get to a point where you can kind of just rest in God's presence.

226
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,740
And I don't know that I fully agree with that,

227
00:15:00,780 --> 00:15:03,800
because as I was studying and thinking about this,

228
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:07,580
I got to observe my baby with my wife.

229
00:15:07,580 --> 00:15:11,040
And Rory has not the maturity to talk,

230
00:15:11,040 --> 00:15:13,360
nor the maturity to listen.

231
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:15,620
But I tell you what,

232
00:15:15,620 --> 00:15:18,380
when that kid gets in between a rock and a hard place,

233
00:15:18,380 --> 00:15:22,020
he throws himself into the presence of his mother.

234
00:15:22,020 --> 00:15:28,820
He knows where to go when stress, anxiety, fear, difficulty face his life.

235
00:15:28,820 --> 00:15:32,700
And I think there's something that has to do with what Jesus said,

236
00:15:32,700 --> 00:15:34,200
that we need a childlike faith.

237
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:38,540
That some of us, we've matured so far beyond that.

238
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:39,940
We're so smart.

239
00:15:39,940 --> 00:15:41,800
We know so many passages of Scripture.

240
00:15:41,800 --> 00:15:43,440
We can quote so many things.

241
00:15:43,440 --> 00:15:46,620
We've got our systematic theology just rooted down.

242
00:15:46,620 --> 00:15:50,840
We're too mature to throw ourselves into the presence of God.

243
00:15:50,840 --> 00:15:56,080
And I just can't help but think that today,

244
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:58,740
God is extending to all of us an invitation.

245
00:15:58,740 --> 00:16:02,120
Not a legalistic requirement.

246
00:16:02,120 --> 00:16:05,060
Not a religious thing that you have to check the right box.

247
00:16:05,060 --> 00:16:06,540
You have to do it for the right amount of time,

248
00:16:06,540 --> 00:16:07,740
the right amount of days a week.

249
00:16:08,120 --> 00:16:12,080
It's an invitation to throw yourself into the presence of God.

250
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:16,140
So, how do we develop a rhythm of prayer

251
00:16:16,140 --> 00:16:18,580
that allows us to rest in God's presence?

252
00:16:18,580 --> 00:16:22,920
I've got four steps we're going to cover for the rest of our time.

253
00:16:22,920 --> 00:16:24,700
I couldn't make them spell anything.

254
00:16:24,700 --> 00:16:25,500
I really tried.

255
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:25,940
I'm sorry.

256
00:16:25,940 --> 00:16:29,600
I know, if I was a good pastor, I would have figured it out.

257
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:31,200
But pause, number one, pause.

258
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:32,840
Number two, surrender.

259
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:34,620
Number three, contemplate.

260
00:16:34,620 --> 00:16:36,840
And number four, receive.

261
00:16:37,240 --> 00:16:40,180
This is not a silver bullet to euphoria.

262
00:16:40,180 --> 00:16:43,580
This is not, if you do the right things in the right order,

263
00:16:43,580 --> 00:16:44,660
everything is perfect.

264
00:16:44,660 --> 00:16:47,120
This is just four steps that I think,

265
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:50,620
if we regularly enter into the presence of God with these four steps,

266
00:16:50,620 --> 00:16:54,340
if we're able to pause, surrender, contemplate, and receive,

267
00:16:54,340 --> 00:16:58,840
I think that God will show up and give us genuine rest.

268
00:16:59,840 --> 00:17:00,840
So, number one, pause.

269
00:17:00,840 --> 00:17:04,420
Psalm 46, verses 10 and 11.

270
00:17:04,420 --> 00:17:11,220
Be still and know that I am God.

271
00:17:11,220 --> 00:17:15,080
I will be honored by every nation.

272
00:17:15,080 --> 00:17:18,060
I will be honored throughout the world.

273
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:31,560
Be still and know that the creator of the universe is still on the throne

274
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:35,180
and that he's sovereign over all of your problems and your worries and your anxieties.

275
00:17:35,620 --> 00:17:39,020
The first step to contemplative prayer is just to pause.

276
00:17:39,020 --> 00:17:43,400
Find a quiet and comfortable place that you can get alone

277
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:46,120
and take a few big, deep breaths.

278
00:17:46,120 --> 00:17:47,440
People get weird about this.

279
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:48,620
It's just science.

280
00:17:48,620 --> 00:17:51,260
It's good for your body to breathe from your diaphragm.

281
00:17:51,260 --> 00:17:53,800
Most of us are so stressed, worried, anxious, hurried,

282
00:17:53,800 --> 00:17:55,460
that we never get belly breaths in.

283
00:17:56,460 --> 00:17:58,240
Okay, there's nothing weird about this.

284
00:17:58,240 --> 00:18:00,700
It's just breathe the way God created you to breathe.

285
00:18:00,700 --> 00:18:01,760
All right, let's do that.

286
00:18:01,760 --> 00:18:03,920
Let's relax a little bit.

287
00:18:03,920 --> 00:18:04,560
Pause.

288
00:18:04,560 --> 00:18:05,460
No phones.

289
00:18:05,460 --> 00:18:06,800
No distractions.

290
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:10,640
I'm just going to get real vulnerable with you.

291
00:18:10,640 --> 00:18:14,500
Even if my phone's in the other room and I hear it vibrate, I'm gone.

292
00:18:14,500 --> 00:18:15,240
Like, it's over.

293
00:18:15,240 --> 00:18:16,800
My pausing is done.

294
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:17,960
And so find something.

295
00:18:17,960 --> 00:18:18,680
Do not disturb.

296
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:19,600
Whatever it is.

297
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:21,680
And find a comfortable place.

298
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:23,460
There's different places for different people.

299
00:18:23,460 --> 00:18:26,380
Favorite chair, porch swing, garden.

300
00:18:27,180 --> 00:18:29,480
I grew up with a dad that fished a lot.

301
00:18:29,480 --> 00:18:33,400
And he would say at times, sometimes I feel closer to God on the water

302
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:35,320
than I do in the sanctuary of a church.

303
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:37,240
Anybody?

304
00:18:37,240 --> 00:18:41,300
Find that place for you to relax and to pause.

305
00:18:41,300 --> 00:18:43,760
And if you're a mother of young children,

306
00:18:43,760 --> 00:18:46,560
maybe you just have to pretend like you're going to the bathroom

307
00:18:46,560 --> 00:18:47,820
for a bit longer than normal.

308
00:18:47,820 --> 00:18:52,400
Maybe you pull your car into the driveway,

309
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:55,680
or before you get to the driveway, you pull into somebody else's driveway.

310
00:18:56,460 --> 00:19:01,820
And you just like 10 minutes in the car and let your husband not know

311
00:19:01,820 --> 00:19:05,000
that you're done with whatever chore or errand you were doing.

312
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,380
Just close your eyes.

313
00:19:06,380 --> 00:19:12,380
Take a few deep breaths and acknowledge God's presence in your life.

314
00:19:13,760 --> 00:19:16,500
See, most of us, many of us, I won't say most of us,

315
00:19:16,500 --> 00:19:18,060
I'll throw myself under the bus here,

316
00:19:18,060 --> 00:19:20,460
even mature disciples of Jesus,

317
00:19:20,460 --> 00:19:23,020
we often live as functional atheists.

318
00:19:23,020 --> 00:19:27,100
We don't acknowledge God's presence in our every moment lives.

319
00:19:27,100 --> 00:19:28,700
We get stressed and overwhelmed.

320
00:19:28,700 --> 00:19:31,720
Our eyes, we're Peter, stepping out to the water,

321
00:19:31,720 --> 00:19:35,260
and then everything else distracts us away from the presence of God.

322
00:19:36,060 --> 00:19:38,600
And so this moment to pause is just a moment to acknowledge

323
00:19:38,600 --> 00:19:40,080
the thing that's always been true.

324
00:19:40,080 --> 00:19:42,320
God is present with you.

325
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:47,220
But how often do we live as if he's not?

326
00:19:47,220 --> 00:19:49,060
I love what Peter Greig says.

327
00:19:49,060 --> 00:19:51,420
He says, it's not that God's not present to you,

328
00:19:51,420 --> 00:19:53,820
it's that you are absent to God.

329
00:19:53,820 --> 00:19:58,180
And this time of pausing and just acknowledging God's presence

330
00:19:58,180 --> 00:20:01,740
is a moment for us to reflect on something that's always been true,

331
00:20:01,860 --> 00:20:04,300
but we have oftentimes been living as if it isn't.

332
00:20:04,300 --> 00:20:05,880
So we pause.

333
00:20:05,880 --> 00:20:07,460
We acknowledge God's presence.

334
00:20:07,460 --> 00:20:09,180
I love how Hebrews chapter 10 puts it.

335
00:20:09,180 --> 00:20:10,100
This is so powerful.

336
00:20:10,100 --> 00:20:11,000
Don't miss this.

337
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:12,840
So, dear brothers and sisters,

338
00:20:12,840 --> 00:20:17,320
we can boldly enter heaven's most holy place

339
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:19,440
because of the blood of Jesus.

340
00:20:19,440 --> 00:20:24,400
We enter God's presence because of what Jesus has done for us.

341
00:20:24,400 --> 00:20:28,780
By his death, Jesus opened a new and life-giving way

342
00:20:28,780 --> 00:20:32,380
through the curtain into the most holy place.

343
00:20:32,380 --> 00:20:36,380
And since we have a great high priest who rules over God's house,

344
00:20:36,380 --> 00:20:38,820
let us go right into the presence of God

345
00:20:38,820 --> 00:20:42,000
with sincere hearts, fully trusting him.

346
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:45,460
For our guilty conscience has been sprinkled with Christ's blood

347
00:20:45,460 --> 00:20:46,300
to make us clean,

348
00:20:46,300 --> 00:20:48,340
and our bodies have been washed with pure water.

349
00:20:48,340 --> 00:20:51,760
No matter where you are in your life,

350
00:20:51,760 --> 00:20:54,760
no matter what patterns and habitual sins

351
00:20:54,760 --> 00:20:56,180
that you are struggling with,

352
00:20:57,180 --> 00:21:02,120
you have confident, bold access into the presence of God.

353
00:21:02,120 --> 00:21:05,240
God created you for that type of presence.

354
00:21:05,240 --> 00:21:07,140
He's invited you into that presence.

355
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:12,300
And the author of Hebrews here mentions the old way,

356
00:21:12,300 --> 00:21:15,560
that just the Levite priest once a year

357
00:21:15,560 --> 00:21:18,520
would have the opportunity to enter into the presence of God.

358
00:21:18,520 --> 00:21:21,840
But because of Jesus' blood, his death, burial, and resurrection,

359
00:21:21,840 --> 00:21:26,620
you and I have bold confidence to enter the presence of God

360
00:21:26,620 --> 00:21:28,600
as children of God.

361
00:21:28,600 --> 00:21:31,100
I remember when I was,

362
00:21:31,100 --> 00:21:33,940
for a while,

363
00:21:33,940 --> 00:21:36,680
college and some other years,

364
00:21:36,680 --> 00:21:40,420
I had a on and off addiction to pornography, right?

365
00:21:41,640 --> 00:21:44,120
And I remember when I would fail,

366
00:21:44,120 --> 00:21:45,520
when I would fall short,

367
00:21:45,520 --> 00:21:48,920
it was like I needed three or four days away from God

368
00:21:48,920 --> 00:21:53,000
to like make myself feel like I was clean enough

369
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:54,720
to maybe come back into his presence.

370
00:21:54,720 --> 00:21:57,920
And I don't know what you're dealing with in your life,

371
00:21:57,920 --> 00:21:59,720
but I can't help but think there are some of you here

372
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:01,460
who are in patterns of sin,

373
00:22:01,460 --> 00:22:03,200
and you think that that sin

374
00:22:03,200 --> 00:22:06,360
is causing this disconnect between you and God,

375
00:22:06,360 --> 00:22:08,620
that you can't confidently enter his presence.

376
00:22:08,620 --> 00:22:10,100
And I'm just here to tell you this morning,

377
00:22:10,100 --> 00:22:13,340
we are all woefully sinful.

378
00:22:13,340 --> 00:22:15,460
Our hearts are deceitful and wicked.

379
00:22:15,460 --> 00:22:18,300
And we all, right now, today,

380
00:22:18,300 --> 00:22:19,640
no matter what we've done,

381
00:22:19,640 --> 00:22:21,840
have boldness to enter the presence of God

382
00:22:21,840 --> 00:22:23,520
because of what Jesus has done.

383
00:22:23,520 --> 00:22:26,960
Do not neglect Christ's sacrifice

384
00:22:26,960 --> 00:22:29,440
by refusing to receive the forgiveness

385
00:22:29,440 --> 00:22:30,840
that he's freely given to you.

386
00:22:30,840 --> 00:22:34,460
With boldness, enter God's presence

387
00:22:34,460 --> 00:22:37,140
day in and day out.

388
00:22:38,280 --> 00:22:41,060
How often do we actually enter God's presence

389
00:22:41,060 --> 00:22:42,680
with this boldness and acknowledge it?

390
00:22:42,680 --> 00:22:45,820
Honestly, this is the hardest step of the process.

391
00:22:45,820 --> 00:22:48,960
Getting time to pause, right?

392
00:22:48,960 --> 00:22:52,400
The other three steps, if you have time to pause,

393
00:22:52,400 --> 00:22:54,440
if you get away for a few minutes,

394
00:22:54,440 --> 00:22:56,260
get the phone off,

395
00:22:56,260 --> 00:22:58,060
somebody else is taking care of the kids,

396
00:22:58,060 --> 00:23:00,240
the other three steps are pretty easy,

397
00:23:00,240 --> 00:23:02,820
but the enemy wants nothing more

398
00:23:02,820 --> 00:23:04,680
than to keep you from getting to the first step.

399
00:23:04,680 --> 00:23:04,940
Yeah.

400
00:23:07,940 --> 00:23:10,860
Dallas Willard, Christian philosopher,

401
00:23:10,860 --> 00:23:11,860
was once asked,

402
00:23:11,860 --> 00:23:15,540
what's the greatest enemy to spiritual health

403
00:23:15,540 --> 00:23:16,260
in our culture?

404
00:23:16,260 --> 00:23:18,540
He paused for a minute and he responded,

405
00:23:18,540 --> 00:23:22,980
ruthlessly eliminate hurry from your life.

406
00:23:22,980 --> 00:23:26,660
Hurry is the great enemy of the spiritual life.

407
00:23:26,660 --> 00:23:44,740
Any of us uncomfortable with silence?

408
00:23:44,740 --> 00:23:44,880
Silence.

409
00:23:44,880 --> 00:23:51,580
See, most of us,

410
00:23:51,580 --> 00:23:53,160
when we get alone by ourselves,

411
00:23:53,540 --> 00:23:55,540
we will be distracted.

412
00:23:55,540 --> 00:23:59,000
We will be overwhelmed by thoughts

413
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:00,360
and feelings and distractions.

414
00:24:00,360 --> 00:24:04,100
We'll be uncomfortable just sitting in silence.

415
00:24:04,100 --> 00:24:10,060
And I think it's because we do have this propensity

416
00:24:10,060 --> 00:24:12,420
to fill our lives with busy and hurry.

417
00:24:13,300 --> 00:24:16,600
We avoid any silence at all

418
00:24:16,600 --> 00:24:19,060
because we're afraid of what we might think

419
00:24:19,060 --> 00:24:20,780
or feel or hear from the Lord.

420
00:24:20,780 --> 00:24:23,100
And I just,

421
00:24:23,100 --> 00:24:26,400
I think we've got to get over that.

422
00:24:26,400 --> 00:24:31,080
I think we've got to plunge into the scariness

423
00:24:31,080 --> 00:24:32,480
of the silence.

424
00:24:32,480 --> 00:24:35,920
Be alone with ourselves and with God

425
00:24:35,920 --> 00:24:37,360
and allow him to do the work

426
00:24:37,360 --> 00:24:38,460
that only he can do

427
00:24:38,460 --> 00:24:40,620
when we eliminate the hurry and the distractions.

428
00:24:41,660 --> 00:24:42,340
See, Adam and Eve,

429
00:24:42,340 --> 00:24:43,160
after the fall,

430
00:24:43,160 --> 00:24:45,860
God did what God did.

431
00:24:45,860 --> 00:24:49,320
He walked in the garden in the cool of night

432
00:24:49,320 --> 00:24:52,120
wanting to be with Adam and Eve.

433
00:24:52,120 --> 00:24:56,600
They got busy making clothes,

434
00:24:56,600 --> 00:24:58,040
blaming each other and hiding.

435
00:24:58,040 --> 00:25:00,060
From that point on,

436
00:25:00,060 --> 00:25:02,520
I believe one of humanity's tactics,

437
00:25:02,520 --> 00:25:04,560
one of our fleshly tactics

438
00:25:04,560 --> 00:25:06,340
to avoid God's presence

439
00:25:06,340 --> 00:25:08,120
is busyness and hurry.

440
00:25:08,800 --> 00:25:10,840
And Jesus is inviting us to pause

441
00:25:10,840 --> 00:25:12,940
and to acknowledge his presence.

442
00:25:12,940 --> 00:25:16,320
And if you're anything like me

443
00:25:16,320 --> 00:25:18,140
and you're just successful at this,

444
00:25:18,140 --> 00:25:19,820
immediately.

445
00:25:19,820 --> 00:25:23,040
Distraction, distraction, distraction.

446
00:25:23,040 --> 00:25:24,460
What's for dinner?

447
00:25:24,460 --> 00:25:25,860
Who's picking up the kid?

448
00:25:25,860 --> 00:25:27,520
Did I pay that bill?

449
00:25:27,520 --> 00:25:30,940
Is there enough money

450
00:25:30,940 --> 00:25:32,900
getting put into my Roth IRA account?

451
00:25:32,900 --> 00:25:34,360
Do I have enough life insurance

452
00:25:34,360 --> 00:25:35,880
to cover if something bad happens?

453
00:25:36,120 --> 00:25:36,740
These are mine.

454
00:25:36,740 --> 00:25:37,600
I don't know what yours are,

455
00:25:37,600 --> 00:25:38,320
but there you go.

456
00:25:38,320 --> 00:25:38,900
Now you know.

457
00:25:38,900 --> 00:25:40,280
Right?

458
00:25:40,280 --> 00:25:41,360
Pause.

459
00:25:41,360 --> 00:25:43,040
Step two is surrender.

460
00:25:43,040 --> 00:25:45,420
As these anxious thoughts

461
00:25:45,420 --> 00:25:47,700
fill your mind and your heart,

462
00:25:47,700 --> 00:25:49,520
we lay them at the feet of Jesus.

463
00:25:49,520 --> 00:25:51,740
Let's read the rest of Psalm 46.

464
00:25:51,740 --> 00:25:53,600
Starting in verse one,

465
00:25:53,680 --> 00:25:55,560
God is our refuge and our strength,

466
00:25:55,560 --> 00:25:57,640
always ready to help

467
00:25:57,640 --> 00:25:59,300
in times of trouble.

468
00:25:59,300 --> 00:26:01,620
So we will not fear

469
00:26:01,620 --> 00:26:02,980
when earthquakes come

470
00:26:02,980 --> 00:26:04,280
and when mountains crumble

471
00:26:04,280 --> 00:26:05,020
into the sea.

472
00:26:05,020 --> 00:26:07,520
Let the oceans roar and foam.

473
00:26:07,520 --> 00:26:08,720
Let the mountains tremble

474
00:26:08,720 --> 00:26:10,320
as the waters surge.

475
00:26:10,320 --> 00:26:13,140
A river brings joy

476
00:26:13,140 --> 00:26:13,980
to the city of God,

477
00:26:13,980 --> 00:26:14,900
the sacred home

478
00:26:14,900 --> 00:26:15,580
of the Most High.

479
00:26:15,580 --> 00:26:17,020
God dwells in that city.

480
00:26:17,020 --> 00:26:18,260
It cannot be destroyed.

481
00:26:19,340 --> 00:26:20,940
From the very break of day,

482
00:26:20,940 --> 00:26:21,880
God will protect it.

483
00:26:21,880 --> 00:26:23,300
The nations are in chaos

484
00:26:23,300 --> 00:26:24,460
and their kingdoms crumble.

485
00:26:24,460 --> 00:26:25,600
God's voice thunders

486
00:26:25,600 --> 00:26:26,360
and the earth melts.

487
00:26:26,360 --> 00:26:27,640
The Lord of heaven's army

488
00:26:27,640 --> 00:26:28,600
is here among us.

489
00:26:28,600 --> 00:26:29,980
The God of Israel

490
00:26:29,980 --> 00:26:30,680
is our fortress.

491
00:26:30,680 --> 00:26:31,900
Come,

492
00:26:31,900 --> 00:26:33,020
see the glorious works

493
00:26:33,020 --> 00:26:33,500
of the Lord.

494
00:26:33,500 --> 00:26:35,300
See how he brings destruction

495
00:26:35,300 --> 00:26:36,040
upon the world.

496
00:26:36,040 --> 00:26:37,460
He causes wars to end

497
00:26:37,460 --> 00:26:38,160
throughout the earth.

498
00:26:38,160 --> 00:26:39,280
He breaks the bow

499
00:26:39,280 --> 00:26:40,160
and snaps the spear

500
00:26:40,160 --> 00:26:41,180
and he burns the shields

501
00:26:41,180 --> 00:26:41,660
with fire.

502
00:26:42,600 --> 00:26:43,640
I can't help but see

503
00:26:43,640 --> 00:26:46,620
the authors of this psalm

504
00:26:46,620 --> 00:26:49,120
confidently laying out

505
00:26:49,120 --> 00:26:50,340
biblical truth

506
00:26:50,340 --> 00:26:51,400
about God's sovereignty,

507
00:26:51,400 --> 00:26:51,940
his power,

508
00:26:51,940 --> 00:26:52,540
and his strength

509
00:26:52,540 --> 00:26:54,240
and then getting distracted.

510
00:26:54,240 --> 00:26:55,740
Earthquakes,

511
00:26:55,740 --> 00:26:56,920
mountains crumble,

512
00:26:56,920 --> 00:26:58,080
oceans roar,

513
00:26:58,080 --> 00:27:01,680
but God is like a river

514
00:27:01,680 --> 00:27:02,680
running through the sea, right?

515
00:27:02,680 --> 00:27:04,220
Nations are in chaos.

516
00:27:04,220 --> 00:27:05,520
Kingdoms are at war.

517
00:27:05,520 --> 00:27:07,160
Is this how anybody else's

518
00:27:07,160 --> 00:27:08,820
prayer life is like?

519
00:27:08,820 --> 00:27:11,500
And so I can't help but see them

520
00:27:11,500 --> 00:27:12,460
just offering

521
00:27:12,460 --> 00:27:13,800
these distractions,

522
00:27:13,800 --> 00:27:14,540
these worries.

523
00:27:14,540 --> 00:27:15,960
Legitimate worries.

524
00:27:15,960 --> 00:27:16,700
Earthquakes,

525
00:27:16,700 --> 00:27:18,300
that's a legitimate worry,

526
00:27:18,300 --> 00:27:19,260
especially when you live

527
00:27:19,260 --> 00:27:21,340
out in the middle of nowhere

528
00:27:21,340 --> 00:27:22,300
with no protection, right?

529
00:27:22,300 --> 00:27:24,740
Wars, famine,

530
00:27:24,740 --> 00:27:25,560
all of these things

531
00:27:25,560 --> 00:27:26,500
are legitimate worries.

532
00:27:26,500 --> 00:27:29,220
But they keep coming back

533
00:27:29,220 --> 00:27:29,980
to God's presence.

534
00:27:29,980 --> 00:27:31,600
They keep reminding themselves

535
00:27:31,600 --> 00:27:32,820
of what they know to be true

536
00:27:32,820 --> 00:27:34,460
even though they're caused

537
00:27:34,460 --> 00:27:35,840
to be distracted.

538
00:27:35,840 --> 00:27:38,220
This psalm is littered

539
00:27:38,220 --> 00:27:39,240
with confident faith

540
00:27:39,240 --> 00:27:40,260
in the promises of God

541
00:27:40,260 --> 00:27:41,280
mixed with distractions

542
00:27:41,280 --> 00:27:42,000
and acknowledgement

543
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:43,240
of external circumstances.

544
00:27:43,240 --> 00:27:44,740
And if you get away

545
00:27:44,740 --> 00:27:46,440
to a lonely place

546
00:27:46,440 --> 00:27:48,180
to pause to be with God,

547
00:27:48,180 --> 00:27:49,220
your mind and your heart

548
00:27:49,220 --> 00:27:50,500
will be filled with distractions,

549
00:27:50,500 --> 00:27:52,760
worries, anxieties, and fears.

550
00:27:52,760 --> 00:27:53,380
And it's just,

551
00:27:53,380 --> 00:27:54,880
I'm giving you this invitation.

552
00:27:54,880 --> 00:27:55,520
Just lay them

553
00:27:55,520 --> 00:27:56,320
at the feet of Jesus.

554
00:27:56,320 --> 00:27:57,900
Don't try and ignore them.

555
00:27:57,900 --> 00:27:58,540
Don't try and pretend

556
00:27:58,540 --> 00:27:59,220
like they're not there.

557
00:27:59,220 --> 00:28:00,280
Just bring them to God.

558
00:28:00,280 --> 00:28:00,760
Yes, God,

559
00:28:00,760 --> 00:28:01,660
I am worried about

560
00:28:01,660 --> 00:28:02,520
if my Roth IRA

561
00:28:02,520 --> 00:28:03,360
has enough money,

562
00:28:03,360 --> 00:28:04,560
but I believe

563
00:28:04,560 --> 00:28:05,580
that you are a provider,

564
00:28:05,580 --> 00:28:07,460
that you care,

565
00:28:08,620 --> 00:28:10,080
that you're sovereign.

566
00:28:10,080 --> 00:28:12,620
I'm not going to worry

567
00:28:12,620 --> 00:28:13,440
about that right now.

568
00:28:13,440 --> 00:28:14,400
I'm going to trust you.

569
00:28:14,400 --> 00:28:15,940
I heard a quote

570
00:28:15,940 --> 00:28:17,360
the past week

571
00:28:17,360 --> 00:28:17,820
that said,

572
00:28:17,820 --> 00:28:19,240
stress is taking ownership

573
00:28:19,240 --> 00:28:20,020
over something

574
00:28:20,020 --> 00:28:20,800
that you don't have

575
00:28:20,800 --> 00:28:21,520
authority over.

576
00:28:21,520 --> 00:28:23,920
How many of us

577
00:28:23,920 --> 00:28:24,760
